# AdmissionHack — backend (optional)
#
# Leave these unset and the whole product still works: the workspace lives in the
# browser and nothing is uploaded. Setting them enables accounts, cloud sync and
# the counselor view.
#
# Apply the schema first. It lives in the shared ecosystem project (sathack), not
# a dedicated one, so the combined file is the one that matters:
#   supabase/ecosystem-migration.sql   — tables, RLS, buckets, folders, groups
# (0003_application_tracker.sql is the tracker's additive follow-up.)
#
# Use the project's publishable key (sb_publishable_…) rather than the legacy
# anon JWT: it is what Supabase recommends for new apps and can be rotated on its
# own. Both values are public — they ship to the browser — and grant only what the
# RLS policies allow, which is nothing at all until a user signs in.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional. The site's own origin, used to build sitemap.xml. While the domain is
# undecided it falls back to a placeholder; set this to the real one (no trailing
# slash) when deploying, and rebuild — a static sitemap is generated at build time.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# AI essay reviewer. Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint works, so
# the vendor is configuration rather than code — the provider has already changed
# once and should not cost a code edit again.
#
# Server-side ONLY: there is deliberately no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, because that
# would ship the key to every visitor's browser. Leave it unset and the writing
# tab says the reviewer is not configured rather than showing a form that fails.
#
# Defaults are DeepSeek. To move to Zhipu GLM instead, set
#   AI_API_BASE_URL=https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4
#   AI_MODEL=glm-4.6
# To move to OpenAI:
#   AI_API_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#   AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# The account needs credit. An uncredited key still authenticates but every
# completion fails — DeepSeek says so with 402, Zhipu with 429 + code 1113 — and
# the route reports both as "upstream_quota" rather than as a rate limit.
#
# Model choice, measured rather than assumed: `deepseek-chat` (the stable alias,
# currently served by DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash) returns the structured review cleanly,
# in well under a second. `deepseek-v4-pro` answers 200 with EMPTY content for
# this request shape, so the route reports bad_model_output — do not switch to it
# without testing that first.
AI_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults: https://api.deepseek.com and deepseek-chat
AI_API_BASE_URL=
AI_MODEL=
